                                <div class=3D"ct-publish-body" style=3D"hei=
ght: auto !important;">
                                    The article explains how to install a n=
ewer version of=E2=80=AFNginx on Ubuntu=E2=80=AF20.04 by either using the d=
efault Ubuntu package (stable=E2=80=AF1.18) for a quick, =E2=80=9Cgood=E2=
=80=91enough=E2=80=9D setup or adding the official nginx.org repository to =
obtain the latest stable (=E2=89=881.22) or mainline (=E2=89=881.23) releas=
es with extra features. It walks through adding the signing key, creating s=
eparate source=E2=80=91list files for each branch, updating the package ind=
ex, installing Nginx, verifying the service, and safely rolling back to the=
 Ubuntu version if needed. Throughout, it emphasizes choosing the appropria=
te branch based on risk tolerance=E2=80=94stable for production stability a=
nd mainline for cutting=E2=80=91edge functionality.
                                    <br><br>
                                   =20
<ins class=3D"adsbygoogle" style=3D"display: block; text-align: center; hei=
